\ cv8t-fuse-imm.4 - cv8-fuse-imm.4 under the two-bit tag (Iteration 67, FORMAT-TAG2.md): 64
\ one-byte opcodes and an escape, calls of 2, 3, 4 bytes (14, 22, 30 bits:
\ a 1 GB code space), links of 1-4 bytes. A copy - the original is frozen by
\ the designs recorded with it. The opcode constants keep their logical
\ values here; layout.py --tag2 rewrites each to this design's code.
\ cv8-fuse-imm.4 - n + and SWAP n + in code compiled at RUN time
\ (Iteration 37). Loaded after cv8-fuse.4, and only for designs with the
\ gene rtimm (lab/evolve): its code costs image bytes, and only the
\ designs that choose it pay them.
\
\ The converter makes LIT n + an ADDI n (spec imm) and SWAP n + a SWAP+I n
\ in the image; code the compiler writes at run time had neither - fib's
\ `-1 +` and `SWAP -2 +` were LIT32 n, + and SWAP, LIT32 n, +: three of
\ the thirteen dispatches of each recursive call. Here a literal ADDI can
\ hold leaves LAST-OP pointing at it, and a + compiled straight after
\ takes its place. Safe as the pairs are: every branch target clears
\ LAST-OP; LIT8 and LIT32 are in no fold table and no pair, and a literal
\ is never one byte, so ;8, ?BRANCH, and the pairs pass it by.
\
\ IMM-OPS: this design's ADDI and SWAP+I opcodes (0 where it has none),
\ then its + and SWAP - all four written by the converter
\ (tools/layout.py). A ['] + here would hold the cell system's address,
\ which the converter does not relocate: C@ through it crashed every
\ colon definition.

CREATE IMM-OPS ( --- c-addr )   0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C, 0 C,   \ Iteration 176: DUP+I DUP<I DUP <
ALIGN
VARIABLE LIT-PREV ( --- a-addr )
\ The primitive emitted straight before the last literal, or 0.

: SMALL-LIT? ( a --- n -1 | 0 )
\ The literal at a, ending at HERE, if ADDI's signed byte holds it: LIT8
\ 0-127, or LIT32 -128 to -1 (a negative is never narrower).
  DUP C@ LIT8-OP = IF
    DUP 2 + HERE = IF 1+ C@ DUP 128 < IF -1 EXIT THEN THEN DROP 0 EXIT
  THEN
  DUP C@ LIT32-OP = IF DUP 5 + HERE = IF
    DUP 2 + C@ 255 = OVER 3 + C@ 255 = AND OVER 4 + C@ 255 = AND
    OVER 1+ C@ 128 < 0= AND IF 1+ C@ 256 - -1 EXIT THEN
  THEN THEN DROP 0 ;

: LITERAL8 ( n --- )
\ cv8.4's, and a literal ADDI can hold stays in LAST-OP.
  LAST-OP @ DUP IF DUP 1+ HERE = AND THEN LIT-PREV !
  HERE SWAP LIT,
  IMM-OPS C@ IF DUP SMALL-LIT? IF DROP LAST-OP ! EXIT THEN THEN DROP ; IMMEDIATE

\ Iteration 176: IMM+ with variables - SWAP n + a SWAP+I, DUP n + a DUP+I,
\ n + an ADDI, DUP n < a DUP<I (IMM-OPS bytes 4-7); xt kept when nothing fuses.
VARIABLE IMM-N  VARIABLE IMM-L  VARIABLE IMM-P
: IMM-AT ( a op --- -1 )   \ back to a: the opcode, then the immediate
  SWAP HERE - ALLOT OP, IMM-N @ C, 0 LAST-OP ! -1 ;
: IMM-AFTER ( op --- f )   \ was the operation before the literal op?
  IMM-P @ DUP IF C@ = ELSE SWAP DROP THEN ;
: IMM+ ( xt --- xt 0 | -1 )
  IMM-OPS C@ 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  LAST-OP @ DUP 0= IF EXIT THEN
  DUP IMM-L ! SMALL-LIT? 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN IMM-N !
  LIT-PREV @ IMM-P !
  DUP C@ IMM-OPS 2 + C@ = IF
    IMM-OPS 1+ C@ IF IMM-OPS 3 + C@ IMM-AFTER IF DROP IMM-P @ IMM-OPS 1+ C@ IMM-AT EXIT THEN THEN
    IMM-OPS 4 + C@ IF IMM-OPS 6 + C@ IMM-AFTER IF DROP IMM-P @ IMM-OPS 4 + C@ IMM-AT EXIT THEN THEN
    DROP IMM-L @ IMM-OPS C@ IMM-AT EXIT
  THEN
  IMM-OPS 5 + C@ IF DUP C@ IMM-OPS 7 + C@ = IF
    IMM-OPS 6 + C@ IMM-AFTER IF DROP IMM-P @ IMM-OPS 5 + C@ IMM-AT EXIT THEN
  THEN THEN 0 ;
: COMPILE,8 ( xt --- )
\ cv8-fuse.4's, with n + and SWAP n + tried first.
  DUP >NAME C@ 32 AND IF
    DUP C@ ESC-OP = IF
      DUP C@ OP, 1+ C@ OP, 0 LAST-OP !
    ELSE
      IMM+ IF EXIT THEN
      C@ LAST-OP @ DUP IF DUP 1+ HERE = AND THEN ?DUP IF
        DUP >R C@ OVER SUPER-OP IF SWAP DROP R> C! EXIT THEN R> DROP
      THEN
      HERE LAST-OP ! OP,
    THEN
  ELSE
    CALL,
  THEN ;
